{"title":"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A tennis player computes her win <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ratio\" title=\"Ratio\">ratio</a> by dividing the number of matches she has won by the total number of matches she has played. At the start of a weekend, her win ratio is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba720261b783852a906f780cea358b687c593b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.500$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. During the weekend, she plays four matches, winning three and losing one. At the end of the weekend, her win ratio is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a2894b44a2eb108051bd0de3b9fbc58f63010bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.503$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />. What's the largest number of matches she could've won before the weekend began?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of matches won, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a29c6a83f1cbe4bc785e5879ac0490e5fa2f515a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{2n}=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc4158af32e6b015510d4856aeadfd31d3d4d58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n+3}{2n+4}&gt;\\frac{503}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"118\" height=\"39\" />. \n</p><p>Cross <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiply\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Multiply\">multiplying</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f7e142893dac15ffa0e16e632d785533bef98c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000n+3000&gt;1006n+2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"235\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/941f818cf22bd8debc96519a5370056f0997ae5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;\\frac{988}{6}=164 \\dfrac {4}{6}=164 \\dfrac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"194\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65efc50cfdce1fc11c1d62aecfe83fa381874193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{164}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28same_as_solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(same_as_solution_1)\">Solution 2 (same as solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (same as solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of matches she won before the weekend began. Since her win ratio started at exactly .<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b68eb7380c70b74f9d7b88a963800085bb5d6f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500 = \\tfrac{1}{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"69\" height=\"23\" /> she must have played exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> games total before the weekend began. After the weekend, she would have won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70670f99b13b346e700d7fec74ab5b49061d4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> games out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60ff59acfd1da7566a0009fda6fc3ac319f58f7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> total. Therefore, her win ratio would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/f/d5ffabf0eafd78996be7e38e8211815988381678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+3)/(2n+4).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" /> This means that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/474959c440b3d3ce9e2450a323a5954abf4970c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n+3}{2n+4} &gt; .503 = \\frac{503}{1000}.\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"39\" />Cross-multiplying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c350a94bcb81db54311650d6bc6bb857dc6971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000(n+3) &gt; 503(2n+4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"20\" /> which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd90c243997223aef2f835c6703ffc10c3f0d6bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; \\frac{988}{6} = 164.\\overline{6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"38\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be an integer, the largest possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/431b43631d0829ef085ddb0dce950f19dd8d1188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{164}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"45\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME\" title=\"1992 AIME\">1992 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1992 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</d